          name: Mara Okafor
          role: FLIGHT DIRECTOR
        - id: capcom
          name: Dev Anand
          role: CAPCOM
        - id: navigation
          name: Ilse Brandt
          role: NAVIGATION
        - id: propulsion
          name: Tomas Reyes
          role: PROPULSION
        - id: science
          name: Dr. Amara Nwosu
          role: SCIENCE
        - id: specialist
          name: Jonah Vale
          role: MISSION SPECIALIST
        - id: net
          name: Deep Space Net
          role: AUTOMATED
        lines:
        - id: beacon
          speaker: net
          trigger: 1
          warning: 0
          fault: 0
          delaySeconds: 20
          requiresFlag: 
          forbidsFlag: 
          text: 'MERIDIAN DEEP SPACE NET. CARRIER SEARCH ACTIVE. ANY STATION RECEIVING THIS TRANSMISSION: KEY YOUR TRANSMITTER AND HOLD. ONE-WAY LIGHT TIME {delaymin} MINUTES.'
          replies: []
          storyEvent: 
          logged: 1
          garbled: 0
          requestLabel: 
          requestLine: 
          setsFlag: 
          alreadyOnItsWay: 1
        - id: first_contact
          speaker: capcom
          trigger: 1
          warning: 0
          fault: 0
          delaySeconds: 30
          requiresFlag: 
          forbidsFlag: 
          text: Phainon, Meridian. We have your carrier. We lost you for a long time. Tell us how you are, and remember anything you say takes {delaymin} minutes to get here.
          replies:
          - label: Report status
            line: Meridian, Phainon. Awake. The ship restarted on its own and I am putting it back together. Jupiter is ahead.
            setsFlag: crew_reported
            followUp: contact_reported
          - label: Ask what happened
            line: Meridian, Phainon. I woke up to alarms with most of my flight log gone. What happened to me?
            setsFlag: asked_what_happened
            followUp: contact_asked
          storyEvent: 
          logged: 1
          garbled: 0
          requestLabel: 
          requestLine: 
          setsFlag: 
          alreadyOnItsWay: 0
        - id: contact_reported
          speaker: flight
          trigger: 0
          warning: 0
          fault: 0
          delaySeconds: 20
          requiresFlag: 
          forbidsFlag: 
          text: 'Phainon, Flight. It is good to hear your voice. The plan has not changed: Jupiter first. We will talk about the rest once you are in orbit.'
          replies: []
          storyEvent: 
          logged: 1
          garbled: 0
          requestLabel: 
          requestLine: 
          setsFlag: 
          alreadyOnItsWay: 0
        - id: contact_asked
          speaker: flight
          trigger: 0
          warning: 0
          fault: 0
          delaySeconds: 20
          requiresFlag: 
          forbidsFlag: 
          text: Phainon, Flight. We see the same gap you do. Your telemetry stopped and then came back by itself. We did not command the restart. Say again, we did not -
          replies: []
          storyEvent: 
          logged: 1
          garbled: 1
          requestLabel: 
          requestLine: 
          setsFlag: 
          alreadyOnItsWay: 0
        - id: contact_silent
          speaker: capcom
          trigger: 18
          warning: 0
          fault: 0
          delaySeconds: 5
          requiresFlag: first_contact_no_reply
          forbidsFlag: 
          text: Phainon, Meridian. Nothing heard. We will keep listening for as long as it takes.
          replies: []
          storyEvent: 
          logged: 0
          garbled: 0
          requestLabel: 
          requestLine: 
          setsFlag: 
          alreadyOnItsWay: 0
        - id: capture
          speaker: navigation
          trigger: 25
          warning: 0
          fault: 0
          delaySeconds: 15
          requiresFlag: '@bound'
          forbidsFlag: 
          text: Phainon, Navigation. We show you captured, {peri} by {apo} kilometres. That is an orbit. Well flown.
          replies: []
          storyEvent: objective:capture
          logged: 1
          garbled: 0
          requestLabel: 
          requestLine: 
          setsFlag: 
          alreadyOnItsWay: 0
        - id: regulator_cleared
          speaker: propulsion
          trigger: 20
          warning: 0
          fault: 6
          delaySeconds: 10
          requiresFlag: 
          forbidsFlag: 
          text: Phainon, Reyes. We watched your oxygen regulator stick and we watched you fix it before our warning could reach you. You are {delaymin} minutes ahead of anything we can tell you. Keep that in mind.
          replies: []
          storyEvent: 
          logged: 1
          garbled: 0
          requestLabel: 
          requestLine: 
          setsFlag: 
          alreadyOnItsWay: 0
        - id: science_bands
          speaker: science
          trigger: 25
          warning: 0
          fault: 0
          delaySeconds: 20
          requiresFlag: 
          forbidsFlag: 
          text: Phainon, Science. Your band imagery is down. Nobody in this room has seen the jets from that close. Thank you.
          replies: []
          storyEvent: sent:bands
          logged: 1
          garbled: 0
          requestLabel: 
          requestLine: 
          setsFlag: 
          alreadyOnItsWay: 0
        - id: science_spectrum
          speaker: science
          trigger: 25
          warning: 0
          fault: 0
          delaySeconds: 20
          requiresFlag: anomaly_spectrum
          forbidsFlag: 
          text: Phainon, Science. About your spectrum. There is a line in it that should not be there. Run the instrument again when you can, and hold the result in storage. Do not send that one twice.
          replies: []
          storyEvent: sent:spectrum
          logged: 1
          garbled: 0
          requestLabel: 
          requestLine: 
          setsFlag: 
          alreadyOnItsWay: 0
        - id: complete
          speaker: flight
          trigger: 25
          warning: 0
          fault: 0
          delaySeconds: 30
          requiresFlag: 
          forbidsFlag: 
          text: Phainon, Flight. We have your data. I am cleared to release the next instruction. It is in your log now. I am sorry it is not the one you were hoping for.
          replies: []
          storyEvent: mission_complete
          logged: 1
          garbled: 0
          requestLabel: 
          requestLine: 
          setsFlag: instruction_2_released
          alreadyOnItsWay: 0
        - id: ask_guidance
          speaker: navigation
          trigger: 26
          warning: 0
          fault: 0
          delaySeconds: 15
          requiresFlag: 
          forbidsFlag: '@orbit_stable'
          text: 'Phainon, Navigation. For the capture: NAV MODE to RETRO, GUIDANCE and RCS on, full throttle, and light the engine half a burn before periapsis. You have {dv} metres per second. Cut off when ORBIT GO lights and keep the rest.'
          replies: []
          storyEvent: 
          logged: 1
          garbled: 0
          requestLabel: Ask for capture guidance
          requestLine: Meridian, Phainon. Request guidance for getting into orbit.
          setsFlag: 
          alreadyOnItsWay: 0
        - id: ask_records
          speaker: specialist
          trigger: 26
          warning: 0
          fault: 0
          delaySeconds: 15
          requiresFlag: read:record_instruction
          forbidsFlag: 
          text: Phainon, Vale. Instructions two to nine are sealed until the Jupiter data is on the ground. That was the arrangement you signed. It was written that way for a reason, and I am not allowed to give the reason on this channel.
          replies: []
          storyEvent: 
          logged: 1
          garbled: 0
          requestLabel: Ask about the missing records
          requestLine: Meridian, Phainon. My flight plan shows one instruction out of nine and my log has holes in it. What am I missing?
          setsFlag: 
          alreadyOnItsWay: 0
        - id: ask_objective
          speaker: flight
          trigger: 26
          warning: 0
          fault: 0
          delaySeconds: 15
          requiresFlag: 
          forbidsFlag: 
          text: 'Phainon, Flight. One objective for now: close-range data from a stable orbit, sent home. The bands, the Red Spot, a spectrum, the radiation environment, as many as you can get. Everything after that waits on it.'
          replies: []
          storyEvent: 
          logged: 1
          garbled: 0
          requestLabel: Ask to confirm the objective
          requestLine: Meridian, Phainon. Confirm my objective at Jupiter.
          setsFlag: 
          alreadyOnItsWay: 0
      objectives:
      - id: alarm
        title: Silence the alarm
        stage: WAKING
        text: Alarms. Press MASTER ALARM to silence it, then find out what is wrong.
        control: 19
        condition: 0
        parameter: 
        value: 0
        repairFault: -1
        yieldsToFaults: 0
        setsFlag: 
      - id: power
        title: Restore auxiliary power
        stage: WAKING
        text: The spacecraft is on batteries. Restore the APU.
        control: 32
        condition: 1
        parameter: 
        value: 0
        repairFault: 0
        yieldsToFaults: 0
        setsFlag: 
      - id: cabin
        title: Restart the cabin loop
        stage: WAKING
        text: The cabin is cold and losing pressure. Press CABIN SYS to restart the environment loop.
        control: 13
        condition: 2
        parameter: 
        value: 0
        repairFault: -1
        yieldsToFaults: 0
        setsFlag: 
      - id: nav
        title: Realign the nav platform
        stage: WAKING
        text: The flight computer does not know which way it is pointing. Press NAV SYSTEM to realign the platform.
        control: 11
        condition: 3
        parameter: 
        value: 0
        repairFault: 3
        yieldsToFaults: 0
        setsFlag: 
      - id: radio
        title: Recover the radio link
        stage: WAKING
        text: There is nothing on the radio. Recover the link.
        control: 35
        condition: 4
        parameter: 
        value: 0
        repairFault: 4
        yieldsToFaults: 0
        setsFlag: 
      - id: record
        title: Read the mission record
        stage: TAKING STOCK
        text: The mission computer has recovered part of the flight plan. Press J to open the log and read it.
        control: 0
        condition: 5
        parameter: record_instruction
        value: 0
        repairFault: -1
        yieldsToFaults: 1
        setsFlag: 
      - id: approach
        title: Assess the approach
        stage: JUPITER APPROACH
        text: 'Jupiter is {tpe} away at closest approach, and this path does not stop there. Turn NAV MODE to RETRO: the left display shows the approach and what it takes to stay.'
        control: 52
        condition: 6
        parameter: 
        value: 3
        repairFault: -1
        yieldsToFaults: 1
        setsFlag: 
      - id: propulsion
        title: Pressurise the engine feed
        stage: JUPITER APPROACH
        text: Set FUEL PUMP and TANK PRESS ON and wait for feed pressure.
        control: 33
        condition: 7
        parameter: 
        value: 0
        repairFault: -1
        yieldsToFaults: 1
        setsFlag: 
      - id: attitude
        title: Turn against the flight path
        stage: JUPITER APPROACH
        text: Set GUIDANCE and RCS ON. The computer will turn the engine to face the way you are going.
        control: 36
        condition: 8
        parameter: 
        value: 0
        repairFault: -1
        yieldsToFaults: 1
        setsFlag: 
      - id: capture
        title: Capture into orbit
        stage: JUPITER APPROACH
        text: 'Coast to periapsis: {tpe} to go. Press . to speed time up. Light the engine when TIME TO PE reads {lead}; the burn is {burn} for {capture} m/s of the {dv} you have.'
        control: 0
        condition: 9
        parameter: 
        value: 0
        repairFault: -1
        yieldsToFaults: 1
        setsFlag: captured
      - id: science_power
        title: Power the science payload
        stage: JUPITER ORBIT
        text: In orbit. Set SCIENCE PWR ON to bring the instruments up.
        control: 40
        condition: 10
        parameter: 
        value: 0
        repairFault: -1
        yieldsToFaults: 1
        setsFlag: 
      - id: observe
        title: Collect three observations
        stage: JUPITER ORBIT
        text: 'Collect {need} observations ({count} so far). Choose with INSTRUMENT, aim the window at Jupiter (GUIDANCE off, RCS on, W and S), then press OBSERVE. Payload: {science}.'
        control: 21
        condition: 11
        parameter: 
        value: 3
        repairFault: -1
        yieldsToFaults: 1
        setsFlag: 
      - id: transmit
        title: Send the data home
        stage: JUPITER ORBIT
        text: Press TRANSMIT to send the observations to Earth. The radio link has to hold until the last one has gone.
        control: 22
        condition: 12
        parameter: 
        value: 0
        repairFault: -1
        yieldsToFaults: 1
        setsFlag: 
      instruments:
      - id: camera
        name: IMAGING CAMERA
        label: CAM
        powerWatts: 160
        needsPointing: 1
        pointingToleranceDegrees: 6
        needsSunlight: 1
        condition: 1
      - id: spectrometer
        name: SPECTROMETER
        label: SPEC
        powerWatts: 220
        needsPointing: 1
        pointingToleranceDegrees: 6
        needsSunlight: 1
        condition: 0.8
      - id: radiation
        name: RADIATION SENSOR
        label: RAD
        powerWatts: 60
        needsPointing: 0
        pointingToleranceDegrees: 6
        needsSunlight: 0
        condition: 0.95
      observations:
      - id: bands
        title: Atmospheric band structure
        instrumentId: camera
        durationSeconds: 45
        maxAltitudeMeters: 900000000
        bestAltitudeMeters: 250000000
        needsFeature: 0
        featureWindowDegrees: 55
        finding: An imaging sequence of the zones and belts from close range. Eastward and westward jets alternate with latitude, and the shear between them is drawn out in long streaks of cloud.
        poorFinding: The frames are soft. The belts are there, but little can be measured from them.
        setsFlag: 
        anomaly: 0
        transmitSeconds: 30
      - id: redspot
        title: Great Red Spot
        instrumentId: camera
        durationSeconds: 50
        maxAltitudeMeters: 600000000
        bestAltitudeMeters: 200000000
        needsFeature: 1
        featureWindowDegrees: 55
        finding: The storm fills the frame. Cloud at its rim turns counter-clockwise, and the turbulent wake to its west is laid out in detail.
        poorFinding: The storm is in frame but smeared. Its rim cannot be traced.
        setsFlag: 
        anomaly: 0
        transmitSeconds: 30
      - id: spectrum
        title: Upper atmosphere spectrum
        instrumentId: spectrometer
        durationSeconds: 60
        maxAltitudeMeters: 450000000
        bestAltitudeMeters: 150000000
        needsFeature: 0
        featureWindowDegrees: 55
        finding: Hydrogen, helium, methane and ammonia, where the models put them. One narrow absorption line near 1.74 micrometres matches nothing in the instrument's catalogue. The self-test passes. The line is in every frame.
        poorFinding: The spectrum is noisy. The main gases can be picked out and nothing else can be said.
        setsFlag: anomaly_spectrum
        anomaly: 1
        transmitSeconds: 20
      - id: radiation
        title: Radiation environment
        instrumentId: radiation
        durationSeconds: 60
        maxAltitudeMeters: 500000000
        bestAltitudeMeters: 120000000
        needsFeature: 0
        featureWindowDegrees: 55
        finding: Charged-particle flux rises steeply inward, as it should this deep in the magnetosphere. The dose rate inside the hull is within the limit for the planned stay.
        poorFinding: The counts are too few to draw the profile. The flux rises inward; how steeply is not clear.
        setsFlag: 
        anomaly: 0
        transmitSeconds: 15
      journal:
      - id: record_instruction
        category: 5
        reliability: 0
        title: 'Flight plan: restored from backup'
        body: 'OPERATION PHAINON

          FLIGHT PLAN, RESTORED FROM THE BACKUP STORE


          Instruction 1, current:

          Obtain close-range observation data of Jupiter from a stable orbit. Transmit when able.


          Instructions 2 to 9: NOT RECOVERED.


          Flight history before the restart: 2 entries readable. The number of entries lost is not known.'
        unlockFlag: 
      - id: record_log_fragment
        category: 5
        reliability: 2
        title: 'Flight log: fragment'
        body: '...cruise nominal. I asked again what the second half of the plan is. They said it would be uplinked when [unreadable].


          ...power transient on bus A. Probably nothing. Going to sleep.


          [The entries end here. The date fields did not survive.]'
        unlockFlag: 
      - id: recording_01
        category: 2
        reliability: 1
        title: 'Voice memo: no date stamp'
        body: 'A recording in the personal store. The voice is your own.


          "If you are hearing this, the restart worked, and you do not remember making this. They said that might happen.


          Do the Jupiter work first. I cannot tell you the rest, because I do not know it either. I only know that I agreed to it."


          There is no date on the file and nothing to say when, or whether, it was recorded on this flight.'
        unlockFlag: done:cabin
      - id: record_instruction_2
        category: 5
        reliability: 0
        title: 'Flight plan: instruction 2'
        body: 'INSTRUCTION 2, RELEASED BY UPLINK


          Do not begin the return. Hold at Jupiter. A second target will be given.


          Instructions 3 to 9: SEALED.'
        unlockFlag: instruction_2_released
      faults:
      - fault: 6
        afterObjectiveId: capture
        delaySeconds: 420
      orbitMinPeriapsisMeters: 5000000
      orbitMaxApoapsisMeters: 3000000000
      escapeFailRadiusMeters: 700000000
      burnWindowWarningSeconds: 300
      completionText: 'The Jupiter data is on its way home. The flight plan still shows one instruction of nine. The spacecraft is yours: stay in orbit, keep observing, or save and rest from the pause menu.'
